The function `LastIndexOf` can return a value larger than the size of the list in case no match was found in the reversed range. This happens when the `LastIndexOf` method tries to search backwards from the end of the range where no match found. As a result, `RET` is not defined in this case, because there's no return value for the reversed range, so the return-value assertion in the `LastIndexOf` method should not fail even if the `RET` is not defined in this case.--------------------